args: opentide --json setup vscode --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Recommend the opentide extension and write snippets. Default: both.

The recommended way to use opentide in VS Code is the opentide extension (opentidehq.opentide, on the VS Code Marketplace and Open VSX). It bundles opentide, so nothing else is installed. This command is an alternative for setups without it.

Usage: opentide setup vscode [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -C, --path <PATH_FLAG>
          Repository path
          
          [default: .]

      --settings
          Recommend the opentide extension in .vscode/extensions.json, and remove opentide's yaml.schemas from .vscode/settings.json

      --snippets
          Write object template snippets

      --no-merge
          Replace extensions.json instead of merging

      --no-generate
          Do not run opentide generate first

      --mcp
          Also write .vscode/mcp.json (same as setup mcp --vscode)

  -y, --yes
          Accepted for symmetry with other setup subcommands; this command never prompts

      --plan
          List the files each step would write, and write nothing

      --help
          Print help

Install the extension (recommended):
  $ code --install-extension opentidehq.opentide

Examples:
  $ opentide setup vscode --settings

━━━ stderr · empty
